Template: homelab-agent/api_base
Type: string
Default: http://localhost:3000
Description: Base URL where homelab-api is reachable:
 Written into config.yml's homelab_api.base_url. Also used once, at
 first install, to redeem the enrollment code below.

Template: homelab-agent/hostname
Type: string
Default:
Description: This host's own logical name (e.g. "ct07"):
 Keyed against in api.hosts/api.host_service_status and shown in
 `homelab-cli fleet status`. Leave blank to use this system's own
 hostname (hostname -s) as a default.

Template: homelab-agent/advertise_host
Type: string
Default: 127.0.0.1
Description: This host's own reachable address:
 Written into config.yml's advertise_host -- what homelab-api connects
 to for an on-demand live GET /status (an admin's own real-time
 check), separate from the periodic heartbeat this agent pushes out.
 Leave as 127.0.0.1 only if nothing outside this host will ever need
 the pull path.

Template: homelab-agent/listen_port
Type: string
Default: 2520
Description: Port for homelab-agent to listen on:

Template: homelab-agent/enrollment_code
Type: password
Default:
Description: One-time enrollment code for this host:
 Obtain this from a site_admin BEFORE installing, via
 `homelab-cli admin agent enroll <hostname>` run on an already-enrolled
 admin session. Single-use and short-lived (10 minutes by default) --
 exchanged once, at first install, for this agent's own long-lived
 identity; never stored or reused after that. Leave blank to skip
 enrollment for now (the service will refuse to start until you run
 `dpkg-reconfigure homelab-agent` with a real code).
